From 97b3571a6d8ed51ebc0215b9b10da597a0aa7740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:48:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C2 input-side checkers: input-authorization tier screen,
 narrative-legitimacy screen, C2 rollup

Dimension 2 -- input-authorization tier screen (regulatory_checks.py):
7-tier ladder (T0 prohibited .. T6 vendor-opaque) parameterized per
regulation via RegulationCheckProfile.authorized_inputs/tier_floor/
prohibited_inputs, same declared-name-screen posture as
check_proxy_variables -- works whether an industry has a real filed-
variable list, only a blacklist, or nothing at all. Every tier claim
carries a stacked confidence label (undeclared -> attested-unsupported
-> attested-accountable-unsupported -> attested-accountable-evidenced
-> verified) via TierDeclaration, reusing the ledger's authorized_by
field and cassette_schema's approval_date/justification/last_reviewed
metadata-slot names rather than inventing new ones. Jurisdiction
conflict rule (stricter tier wins) implemented as resolve_tier_conflict.

Dimension 3 -- narrative-legitimacy screen: Phase A (always runs)
reports not_screened when a regulation declares narrative_field and
the decision doesn't carry it, closing the silent-never-fires gap.
Phase B screens narrative text for narrative_flag_phrases and
cross-references against mismatched_fields (deviation) and reasons
(explained vs. unexplained) to flag a possible laundered reason.

Build item 3 -- C2 rollup: rollup_c2_bias_identification combines
findings across dimensions into PASS/FLAG/INDETERMINATE per the
AND-rollup rule; INDETERMINATE (any applicable dimension not yet
evaluated) takes precedence over FLAG, so a lending-shaped rollup that
includes the still-blocked dimension 4 (statistical outcome-equity)
stays honestly INDETERMINATE regardless of how clean 1-3 come back.

Disclosed, not attempted: variable renaming defeats both the proxy and
tier screens (documented in module docstring, same class as the
pre-existing latent-proxy gap); narrative screen is English-only and
cannot catch a sufficiently disconnected fabricated reason.

Not wired into the shipped CFPB/Reg-B reference lens this session --
left as tested, documented profile extensions (RegulationCheckProfile
fields + standalone checker functions) rather than bumping the lens's
version to add checks the build prompt didn't ask it to carry.

Tests: new Tests/test_c2_input_side_checkers.py (24 tests, no Postgres
needed -- pure DecisionMaterial/profile logic). Full regression:
365/365 (341 baseline + 24 new), including the existing
Tests/test_regulatory_cassettes.py suite unmodified and green.

regulatory_cassettes/README.md updated to document the two new checks,
the rollup, and the updated out-of-scope list.
